WEBVTT

00:05.670 --> 00:13.440
Will come back early in the course they talked about building a skyscraper a skyscraper could be a project

00:13.560 --> 00:15.610
would be a really big project.

00:15.720 --> 00:18.260
When you consider all the different moving parts.

00:18.260 --> 00:26.460
So we have you know the foundation of that skyscraper the excavation of the metal's deal with the steel

00:26.460 --> 00:33.090
beams and the framing there and the glass the elevators the interior all of the different things that

00:33.090 --> 00:37.490
go into building a skyscraper just mind boggling how all that comes together.

00:37.770 --> 00:42.260
So that could be a project it would be a really big project.

00:42.270 --> 00:50.400
More likely though it would be a program a program where we have multiple related projects that are

00:50.400 --> 00:59.430
managed in orchestration to receive benefits that you would not receive if each project were managed

00:59.430 --> 01:01.250
independent of one another.

01:02.070 --> 01:08.130
So if you think about that skyscraper being a program you can think about the coordination that would

01:08.130 --> 01:11.840
have to happen between all of those different components.

01:11.880 --> 01:21.420
So a program would be one big umbrella if you will of all of those projects and the program manager

01:21.510 --> 01:26.700
would work with the project managers to orchestrate that coordination.

01:26.880 --> 01:29.190
So you think about the delivery of materials.

01:29.190 --> 01:32.830
There's only so much space on that job site for the materials.

01:32.850 --> 01:35.110
So there has to be some logistics there.

01:35.340 --> 01:40.260
And you think about the different resources that are needed electricians that are needed at different

01:40.260 --> 01:44.070
points in that project and at different places in the project.

01:44.100 --> 01:51.480
So the orchestration I keep saying that word because that's really what it is it's managing all of these

01:51.480 --> 01:59.490
different projects with the project managers to receive benefits by scheduling coordinating using logistics

01:59.760 --> 02:01.560
getting to work with one another.

02:01.590 --> 02:03.220
That's program management.

02:03.410 --> 02:12.330
And so Program Management is a related area of project management programs have projects you know project

02:12.330 --> 02:14.790
managers and you have program managers.

02:14.880 --> 02:17.680
So there are multiple related areas.

02:17.870 --> 02:23.490
There is a certification it's a pretty tough certification for program management from PMI.

02:23.490 --> 02:27.020
It's the GMP the program management professional.

02:27.040 --> 02:32.630
There's not a lot of people around the world that have this certification so program management.

02:32.670 --> 02:38.880
The PGE Pete just want to be able to recognize and be familiar with that idea of programs that programs

02:39.270 --> 02:41.290
have projects.

02:41.310 --> 02:41.670
All right.

02:41.700 --> 02:42.460
Good job.

02:42.540 --> 02:44.860
Keep moving forward.
